                        <h1>Craddle of Knowledge</h1>
                        <p>Avatar Growers values the experience with new and existing members. Knowledge <i><span>craddle </span></i>can help you and your organization stay abreast of changes on the platform. We go through great lengths to ensure you are <i><span>knowledgeable </span></i>about your growing experience.</p>
                        <p>For new members we provide you with how to&#39;s, a visual learning experience, and answers to common questions to keep you up to speed on growing changes.</p>
                        <!-- ####################################################################################################### -->
                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions(FAQs)</h2>
                        <p>More than likely someone has asked the same question. Please refer back to the Knowledge Craddle to get the answers you seek.</p>
                        <p>If at any time you are unable to use the self services provided our human representatives will be happy to answer any questions.</p>
                        <!-- ####################################################################################################### -->
                        <h2>Help</h2>
                        <p>Throughout the Craddle you will find the help options where they can point you in the right direction. These help icons can be found on the platform where needed.</p>
                        <!-- ####################################################################################################### -->
                        <h2>How To's</h2>
                        <p>Unsure of how to complete certain aspects of any project, refer to our how-to library of step by step instructions on how to complete any process facilitated by the platform.</p>
                        <p>For new members we provide you with how to&#39;s, a visual learning experience, and answers to common questions to keep you up to speed on the platform.</p>
                        @*<p class="title">@Html.ActionLink("Open", "Open", "Open")</p>*@
                        <!-- ####################################################################################################### -->
                        <h2>More Info</h2>
                        <p>Sometimes it takes a bit more information for members to be clear on topics that are riddled with jargon or ambiguity. We strive to take the guess work out of <span>unfamiliar</span>terms or things that are unclear for all members.</p>
                        @*<p class="title">@Html.ActionLink("Open", "Open", "Open")</p>*@
                        <!-- ####################################################################################################### -->
                        <h2>Resource's</h2>
                        <p>Our resources are generally outside help in addition to what we provide on the platform to get you going in the right direction.</p>
                        <p>Any resource provided on this platform has been vetted for accuracy and deemed beneficial for our members.</p>
                        <p>As with any information we encourage members to provide due dillegence to any resource provider found on this platform.</p>
                        <!-- ####################################################################################################### -->
                        <h2>Videos</h2>
                        <p><em>For visual learners we know that a visual experience <span>makes </span>all the difference. Follow along as we undertake various tasks in complete and precise <span>demonstrations </span>from experienced customers willing to go the extra mile to get their point across. </em></p>
                        <p><em>Many customers benefit from our videos to make their learning process as simple and painless as possible, or for those on the go who need a quick and easy example. </em></p>
                        <!-- ####################################################################################################### -->
                        <h2>Funding Sections</h2>
                        <p>With this platform being one of the first open source organization owned and operated by its members our goal is to create a true equilibrium</p>
                        <p>Funded projects can include Administration,Housing,Education,Community,Finance,Medical and many other services provided to members and participating communities.</p>
                        <p>All funding activities are strictly governed by our various committees who are made up of elected members by and for our members.</p>
                        <p>We live by our commitment to full transparancy of member funding activity for all our members.</p>
                        @*<p class="title">@Html.ActionLink("Open", "Open", "Open")</p>*@
                        <!-- ####################################################################################################### -->
                        <h2>Tracking</h2>
                        <p>Tracking your work can give you some insight on when you can expect to recieve results on induvidual projects.</p>
                        <p>Our members can not only track the progress of their induvidual projects but all member activity.</p>
                        <h3>Payouts</h3>
                        <p>General Payouts are structured for the benefit of our members plan for themselves set in their membership plans and can be accessed on their member dash.</p>
                        <p>Foundational payouts cannot be changed until fully realized by that member. Our vision is that a rising tide lifts all boats so foundational payouts can only be used for the purpose they were designed.</p>
                        <p>Member payouts for certain activities that fall under qualified payouts to be used however the member see fit will be disbursed to their member card.</p>
                        @*<p class="title">@Html.ActionLink("Track Payments", "TrackPayout", "Finance")</p>*@
                        <h2>Approvals</h2>
                        <p>All Activity that affect to overall membership must be approved by our governing body of committees.</p>
                        @*<p class="title">@Html.ActionLink("Track Approvals", "TrackApprovals", "Stakeholder")</p>*@
                        <h2>Topics</h2>
                        <p><em>members now have access to a variety of help articles to help further your understanding of difficult topics and implementations.</em></p>
                       
